# Adding Interactivity (Component)

To handle user input and create a dynamic application, use the `Component` module and the `App` class. Components manage their own state and can be composed using containers.

#include <[ftxui/component/component.hpp](component_8hpp.html)\>

#include <[ftxui/component/app.hpp](app_8hpp.html)\>

#include <[ftxui/dom/elements.hpp](elements_8hpp.html)\>

int [main](examples_2component_2button_8cpp.html#ae66f6b31b5ad750f1fe042a706a4e3d4)() {

using namespace [ftxui](namespaceftxui.html);

std::vector<std::string> entries = {

"Entry 1",

"Entry 2",

"Entry 3",

};

int selected = 0;

// Create a menu component

auto menu = Menu(&entries, &selected);

// You can decorate components using the pipe operator.

auto component = menu | border;

// Start the main loop

auto app = App::TerminalOutput();

app.Loop(component);

return 0;

}

